We can't initialize an empty array on the heap.

In Java, declaring an array as an empty array doesn't work because an empty array is not an object. (In other words, it doesn't have a heap reference to an object.) The compiler requires an array object reference (that will be a variable or parameter) to assign to. The array will be given a size once the program has run and will not allow you to change the size (since a dynamic array would require a special set of operations).

