{% include toc-no-icon.html %}

### What is SARL?

[SARL](https://eclipse-srt.github.io/), or "Software Robotic Thinking Language", is the language that the Sartre Programming Paradigm uses to write concurrent programs. 
See [What is Sartre programming paradigm](/sartre_paradigm)

### What are its goals?

The SARL language, in its original form, has been designed so that it can be read and understood by a programmer (in the 60s of '80s when  started his work on the Sartre Language, that was a little bit later than the 50s of '60s when he started [his work](https://openlanguage.fr/SARL)). The Sartre Language makes it possible to code concurrent programs, while still having a clear structure. 
These goals are: 
* readability by a programmer who is not a programmer
* portability / modularity (because it contains only language constructs)
* low levels (to be easy to read, for everyone)
* ease of learning (with few keywords and conventions)

### What is SARL?

SARL is a language that helps to create code that is easier to understand and write. 

### What is a language / language construct?

A language construct (or language construct, function, component, or method, also called in computer science a *production rule*) is an element that is defined in the grammar of the language itself.
