The program should terminate the dead loop at a specific time if it is still not broken.

Your program can be a Java method, an Ant script or even a make file, as long as:
- The program must be in Java, PHP, Perl, or (even) Python.
- Your program must be able to run on any Linux (and all versions) machine.
- Your program will not be graded in terms of correctness but rather in the performance of your program
(more specifically, the speed of compiling your service).
- Your program must end if the program compiles the service correctly.
- Your program must output a string to STDOUT indicating whether it is currently compiling or not.
