## ClassX & ClassM & ClassW & ClassXW ##

ClassX and ClassM are simple programs that you don't need to understand.
ClassW works and ClassXW works on windows too.

ClassX:
- Works like the `ping` command on Linux
    - You need Python 3 installed because the script needs to get the address of the host you are pinging...
    - You need Net-SSH too.
        - You can use `sudo apt install python3 python3-net-scp` to install it, or you can install it through the installer of Anaconda or pip.
    - The script checks that the host has `ping` support and that `net-ssh` is installed. You can manually override this check by running with `--ignore-check` parameter
- Takes an IP address or a host
    - You can use both a host name or an IP address
    - If you use an IP address, it needs to be of type CIDR, like 192.168.0.0/24
- Does not take a second parameter, so the script will be executed
    - The script will not create the `/etc/classx.config` file to handle the authentication
- I use a default configuration. You can copy `/home/[your username]/.ssh` to `/etc` and edit the `config.ini` inside to work with your own account. Do not add your password or ssh config, just the key file and the ssh server.
- It doesn't support `SSHConfig` file, so there is no way to use a config file... you should use the default config

