## Abstract

KYC-Bot (Key Concepts-based Expert Guided Programming) is a **security-oriented** expert-guided-programming (EGP) framework, which aims at transforming security vulnerability detection and repair into an automated and comprehensive security assessment. KYC-Bot uses the concepts' keywords provided by Google Knowledge Graph to **identify suspicious behaviors to detect vulnerabilities** and automatically translate them into corresponding C code **to be inserted or appended into vulnerable code** to patch them.

## The Problem

One of the major challenges for programmers to become more skilled in software development is **the ever-increasing complexity of modern software systems**. For example, **the most sophisticated software vendors, companies, or organizations rely on automated code generators and code templates** (a.k.a. scaffolding) to **save them time and effort**. However, this kind of code generation has its drawbacks as well. The generated code might not **satisfy any desired requirements, or might be inconsistent with the original design as the code generator generates based on the template**. Thus, a large percentage of generated code will inherently be **subject to security violations**. 

